          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On August 2, 2013 at 23:08, a witness and his wife, driving a car (see map), observed in the clear sky four red-orange glowing points that eventually faded out one after the other. The Meteociel report indicates a light west wind. Observing glowing points in the sky for several minutes on a Saturday night clearly evokes Thai lanterns. Given the location, the objects were slowly moving away from the witnesses towards the East. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\": probable observation of Thai lanterns.",
